from pathlib import Path
import json,html,struct
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];A='/assets/studies/sceye-haps/stage-04';e=html.escape
S=json.loads((B/'results/summary.json').read_text());cs={c['id']:c for c in S};r=cs['reference'];p=cs['pi'];m=p['motor_control'];R=json.loads((B/'verification/refinement.json').read_text());design=json.loads((B/'inputs/controller-design.json').read_text());delta=(p['heater_energy_Wh']-r['heater_energy_Wh'])/1000
rows=''.join(f"<tr><th>{e(c['title'])}</th><td>{c['motor_control']['minimum_housing_C']:.2f}</td><td>{c['motor_control']['peak_heater_W']:.1f} / {c['motor_control']['capacity_W']}</td><td>{c['motor_control']['active_max_abs_error_K']:.3f}</td><td>{c['motor_control']['motor_energy_Wh']/1000:.3f}</td><td>{c['heater_energy_Wh']/1000:.3f}</td><td>{c['load_energy_kWh']:.3f}</td><td>{'Meets study criterion' if c['motor_control']['study_tracking_pass'] else 'Misses study criterion'}</td></tr>" for c in S)
thermal=''.join(f'<tr><th>{name}</th><td>{r["node_temperatures"][key]["min_C"]:.2f} to {r["node_temperatures"][key]["max_C"]:.2f}</td><td>{p["node_temperatures"][key]["min_C"]:.2f} to {p["node_temperatures"][key]["max_C"]:.2f}</td></tr>' for key,name in [('propulsion.housing','Motor housing / heater sensor'),('propulsion.winding','Motor winding'),('propulsion.controller','Motor electronics / ESC'),('avionics.cpu','Processor aggregate'),('battery.core','Battery core'),('payload.rf','RF aggregate')])
body=f'''<div class="haps wrap" id="haps-motor" data-base="{A}"><section id="motor-control"><p class="eyebrow">Stage 04 / Motor heater control · same integrated thermal hardware</p><h2>Reach the cold target with room left in the heater.</h2><p>The Stage 03 combined candidate had a 300 W motor heater but a housing minimum of {r['motor_control']['minimum_housing_C']:.2f}°C against its chosen −5°C target. This stage isolates controller tuning: raise proportional gain, then add integral action and anti-windup. The selected PI case reaches a {m['minimum_housing_C']:.2f}°C minimum with {m['peak_heater_W']:.1f} W peak demand and no saturation.</p><div class="haps-jump"><a href="#motor-inputs">1 · Inputs and criteria</a><a href="#motor-steps">2 · Why the change works</a><a href="#motor-explorer">3 · Compare saved runs</a><a href="#motor-checks">4 · Numerical checks</a><a href="#motor-downloads">5 · Models and results</a><a href="#night-control">Previous Stage 03</a></div><p class="h4-warning"><b>Heating control, under explicit study assumptions.</b> The −5°C target and ±0.5 K tracking band are chosen design criteria, not a selected motor’s approved limits. Warm daytime operation remains above the heating target; the heater cannot actively cool it. The hardware and environmental assumptions still require physical correlation.</p></section>
<section id="motor-inputs"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Freeze the plant before tuning the controller</p><h2>What changes, and what is held fixed?</h2><p>The baseline is exactly the <b>Stage 03 combined</b> architecture: temperature-responsive avionics/payload radiator coupling and a 300 W motor heater. All 24 thermal masses, conductances, surface optics, motor electrical losses, wind/mission forcing, heater location and other subsystem controls retain their prior inputs. Changing motor heater power feeds through the common electrical bus and thermal network.</p><div class="h4-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Motor controller input register"><table><thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Stage 03 baseline</th><th>Selected Stage 04 PI</th><th>Basis / scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Housing temperature target</th><td>−5°C</td><td>−5°C</td><td>Chosen heating floor; no supplier allowable inferred.</td></tr><tr><th>Motor heater maximum</th><td>300 W</td><td>300 W</td><td>Same installed-capacity assumption. The separately labeled 100 W case is a capacity diagnostic.</td></tr><tr><th>Proportional gain Kp</th><td>30 W/K</td><td>300 W/K</td><td>P-only 300 W/K case isolates this change before adding integration.</td></tr><tr><th>Integral gain Ki</th><td>0</td><td>2 W/(K·s)</td><td>Three tested values: 0.1, 0.5 and 2; selected Ti=Kp/Ki=150 s. A studied candidate, not a universal optimum.</td></tr><tr><th>Anti-windup tracking time</th><td>Not applicable to P-only</td><td>60 s</td><td>Back-calculation tracks the actual limited power at both 0 and 300 W.</td></tr><tr><th>Sensor / actuator model</th><td>Direct housing temperature; ideal averaged power</td><td>Same nominal sensing/actuation; separate 30 s sensor-lag case</td><td>No noise, bias, PWM, sensor failure or heater electrical/actuator delay is solved.</td></tr><tr><th>Initialization / mission</th><td>Motor nodes initially 20°C; eight continuous days</td><td>Same thermal initialization; integral 0 W; sensor-filter state 20°C</td><td>No controller reset at midnight. The final day is compared only after repeat-cycle checks.</td></tr><tr><th>Chosen acceptance</th><td>Recorded without claiming compliance</td><td>Heater-on |housing−target|≤0.5 K; minimum≥−5.5°C; ≥5% peak power headroom</td><td>Heater-on means delivered power&gt;1 W. Numerical control criteria, not hardware qualification.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a href="{A}/inputs/controller-design.json" download>Controller assumptions and criteria ↓</a> · <a href="#night-inputs">Complete Stage 03 material/load/environment register</a></p></section>
<section id="motor-steps"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Explain the control mechanism</p><h2>Remove the offset without increasing heater capacity.</h2><ol><li><b>Recognize proportional droop.</b> Stage 03 used P=30·(target−temperature). Supplying about 169 W therefore requires about 5.6 K of cold error. Spare heater capacity alone cannot remove that error.</li><li><b>Increase Kp as a controlled comparison.</b> Raising gain to 300 W/K reduces the minimum-temperature error to 0.67 K, but it still needs a nonzero error to sustain heat.</li><li><b>Add an integral correction.</b> Repeated cold error builds a holding-power term. Near the target, that term supplies the heat that offsets environmental losses while the proportional error becomes small.</li><li><b>Limit delivered power and prevent windup.</b> Clamp the heater to 0–300 W. Feed the difference between limited output and raw command back into the integrator, so it accounts for saturation and recovers rather than accumulating an unavailable command.</li><li><b>Choose from the tested gains.</b> With Kp fixed at 300 W/K, the selected Ki=2 keeps all nominal heater-on records within the chosen ±0.5 K band. Slower settings have larger warm-transition tracking errors; compare them instead of assuming any integral term fixes the whole cycle.</li><li><b>Keep the energy consequence visible.</b> Holding the motor warmer takes additional heat. Motor heating rises from {r['motor_control']['motor_energy_Wh']/1000:.3f} to {m['motor_energy_Wh']/1000:.3f} kWh/day. All-heater energy rises from {r['heater_energy_Wh']/1000:.3f} to {p['heater_energy_Wh']/1000:.3f} kWh/day: +{delta:.3f} kWh/day, or {100*(p['heater_energy_Wh']/r['heater_energy_Wh']-1):.1f}%. The original lower consumption accompanied a cold target shortfall.</li></ol><div class="h4-equations">e = Ttarget − Tsensor<br>u = Kp·e + I<br>Pheater = clip(u, 0, Pmax)<br>dI/dt = Ki·e + (Pheater − u) / 60 s</div><p class="haps-small">Positive e requests heat. I is a controller correction in watts, not thermal energy. P and I terms may individually exceed the cap and cancel; only Pheater enters the housing energy balance. The <a href="https://doc.modelica.org/om/Modelica.Blocks.Continuous.LimPID.html">Modelica limited-PI documentation</a> describes the general use of output limits and anti-windup; this downloadable model exposes its own equations explicitly.</p><figure><img src="{A}/review/motor-control-comparison.png" width="2100" height="1350" alt="Native OpenModelica comparison of Stage03 proportional control, higher proportional gain and PI: full and zoomed housing temperature, motor heater power and all-heater energy" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Same nominal mission and 300 W motor heater. Full temperature history remains visible alongside a cold-target zoom; the green band is the chosen ±0.5 K tracking band.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="motor-explorer"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Inspect the saved repeated mission</p><h2>Temperature tracking, heater demand and energy on the same timeline.</h2><div class="haps-box"><div class="h4-controls"><label>Controller / sensitivity<select id="h4-case" aria-label="Motor control case"><option>Loading saved results…</option></select></label><label>Temperature component<select id="h4-node" aria-label="Motor study temperature component"><option value="propulsion.housing">Motor housing / heater sensor</option><option value="propulsion.winding">Motor winding</option><option value="propulsion.controller">Motor electronics / ESC</option><option value="avionics.cpu">Processor aggregate</option><option value="battery.core">Battery core</option><option value="payload.rf">RF aggregate</option></select></label></div><label><input id="h4-overlay" type="checkbox" checked> Overlay the Stage 03 baseline, higher P gain and selected PI in nominal comparisons</label><p id="h4-note" aria-live="polite">Loading native OpenModelica trajectories…</p><div id="h4-stats" class="h4-stats"></div><div class="h4-time"><button id="h4-play">Play day</button><input id="h4-time" type="range" min="0" max="1440" value="0" aria-label="Motor study local solar minute"><output id="h4-time-text">00:00</output></div><div id="h4-now"></div><div class="h4-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Motor study plot"><button data-h4-plot="temperature" aria-pressed="true">Temperature</button><button data-h4-plot="power" aria-pressed="false">Motor heater power</button><button data-h4-plot="motorEnergy" aria-pressed="false">Motor heater energy</button><button data-h4-plot="energy" aria-pressed="false">All heater energy</button><button data-h4-plot="error" aria-pressed="false">Tracking error</button><button data-h4-plot="soc" aria-pressed="false">Battery SOC</button><button data-h4-plot="terms" aria-pressed="false">PI terms</button></div><label id="h4-zoom-label"><input id="h4-zoom" type="checkbox" checked> Cold-target zoom · uncheck for full mission temperature</label><div id="h4-chart"></div><div id="h4-legend"></div><p id="h4-chart-note" class="haps-small"></p><p id="h4-performance" class="haps-small"></p><p class="haps-small">Eight continuous mission days were solved on Intel; the viewer shows the final saved day at 60 s intervals, using post-event interpolation. Playback loops one day in about 24 seconds until paused. Scenario selection inspects saved runs. Colder-air comparisons use the matching cold P-only baseline.</p></div><h3>All nine controlled cases</h3><div class="h4-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Controller case numerical comparison"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Housing minimum°C</th><th>Peak / cap W</th><th>Max heater-on |error| K</th><th>Motor kWh/day</th><th>All heaters kWh/day</th><th>DC kWh/day</th><th>Chosen control criterion</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></div><p class="haps-small">Criterion includes maximum heater-on absolute error, minimum temperature and 5% peak headroom. It is a numerical design criterion. A warmer minimum alone is not enough: the slow integral case heats too far above target during some transitions.</p><details><summary>System and component temperature impacts / same nominal mission</summary><div class="h4-scroll" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Thermal node</th><th>Stage 03 min/max°C</th><th>Selected PI min/max°C</th></tr></thead><tbody>{thermal}</tbody></table></div><p>Housing, winding and motor electronics are separate nodes. Meeting a housing control target does not establish an unknown winding, magnet, bearing, lubricant or ESC allowable. Shared structure and electrical conversion losses transmit small changes to other subsystems.</p></details></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">04 / Stress the chosen setting</p><h2>Colder air and sensor lag retain heater headroom.</h2><p>With air 10 K colder, the selected PI case reaches {cs['cold_pi']['motor_control']['minimum_housing_C']:.2f}°C minimum and {cs['cold_pi']['motor_control']['peak_heater_W']:.1f} W peak demand, leaving {cs['cold_pi']['motor_control']['headroom_W']:.1f} W below the same 300 W cap. Earth/sky IR and wind/load forcing stay fixed, so this is an air-temperature sensitivity rather than a complete cold environmental bound.</p><p>A separate 30 s first-order sensor lag gives {cs['lag_pi']['motor_control']['minimum_housing_C']:.2f}°C minimum. Both sensitivities meet the chosen tracking/headroom criteria. Noise, bias, actuator lag and cold-soaked startup still need separate studies.</p><figure><img src="{A}/review/motor-control-sensitivities.png" width="1950" height="750" alt="Cold-air baseline and PI comparison plus selectedPI with30second sensor lag, showing housing cold-target tracking and heater power below300W" loading="lazy"></figure><p class="h4-warning"><b>The controller cannot create missing capacity.</b> Reducing the same PI-controlled heater to 100 W reaches {cs['undersized']['motor_control']['minimum_housing_C']:.2f}°C and stays capped for {cs['undersized']['motor_control']['at_capacity_h']:.2f} h/day. Its lower energy is a consequence of insufficient delivered heat. This diagnostic also exercises upper-limit anti-windup; it is not a proposed design.</p></section>
<section id="motor-checks"><p class="eyebrow">05 / Check before claiming improvement</p><h2>Native solver results, verified numerically.</h2><ul><li>Reproduce Stage 03 with the PI term disabled before comparing the new controller.</li><li>Check the applied proportional, integral, anti-windup, sensor and limiter equations against native outputs, including the saturated 100 W case.</li><li>Reconstruct every thermal capacity’s storage and independently sum boundary/input/export heat; check the thermal-plus-battery energy balance.</li><li>Compare matching phases of days seven/eight for every thermal node and SOC.</li><li>Refine the selected PI from maximum/output step 60 s and tolerance10⁻⁷ to 30 s and10⁻⁸: maximum common-grid node-temperature change {R['max_temperature_difference_K']:.6f} K and heater-energy change {R['heater_energy_difference_Wh']:.6f} Wh.</li><li>Confirm the native subsystem heat-port connection lists match Stage 03. Controller states add no thermal capacity or hidden heat source.</li></ul><p>These checks establish behavior of the assumed continuous model. Physical tests, selected hardware limits, sensor uncertainty, actual heater switching, faults and a broader environmental envelope remain necessary before hardware decisions.</p></section>
<section id="motor-downloads"><p class="eyebrow">06 / Download and reproduce</p><h2>Controller source, native results and step-by-step report.</h2><div class="h4-downloads"><a href="{A}/Stage-04-Motor-PI-Control-R1.zip" download>Complete Stage 04 source / final-day data / report ZIP ↓</a><a href="{A}/source/HAPSDiurnal.mo" download>Integrated native OpenModelica model ↓</a><a href="{A}/inputs/controller-design.json" download>Controller assumptions and chosen criteria ↓</a><a href="{A}/inputs/cases.json" download>All nine case definitions ↓</a><a href="{A}/docs/Results-Walkthrough.txt" download>Step-by-step report ↓</a><a href="{A}/results/summary.json" download>All case statistics ↓</a><a href="{A}/verification/numerical-audit.json" download>Control / conservation / periodicity audit ↓</a><a href="{A}/verification/refinement.json" download>Selected PI numerical refinement ↓</a><a href="{A}/verification/stage03-reproduction.json" download>Stage 03 reproduction check ↓</a><a href="{A}/source/audit_and_export.py" download>Independent audit and data exporter ↓</a></div><details><summary>Full eight-day native archives / primary comparison and refinement</summary><div class="h4-downloads">{''.join(f'<a href="{A}/native/{i}-full-native.zip" download>{title} / native CSV and log ZIP ↓</a>' for i,title in [('reference','Stage03 P30'),('p300','HigherP300'),('pi','SelectedPI'),('pi_fine','SelectedPI30s refinement')])}</div><p>All nine final-day CSVs and viewer trajectories are in the main ZIP. Complete warm-up/native trajectories for sensitivity and slower-gain cases remain on Intel, with hashes and exact run commands recorded. The archives above retain full native output for the primary comparison and selected refinement.</p></details><p class="haps-small">Open <code>HAPSDiurnal.mo</code> and <code>IntegratedMission</code> in OMEdit, one stage version at a time. All study inputs remain assumed. Native CAD, spatial FEM meshes/fields and the full material register remain in <a href="#night-downloads">Stage 03 downloads</a>.</p></section></div>'''
(B/'source/stage-body.html').write_text(body)
(B/'docs/Results-Walkthrough.txt').write_text('STAGE04 / MOTOR HEATER PI CONTROL\n\nIndependent assumed HAPS model. Heating target−5C is a chosen floor, not a qualified supplier limit.\n\nINPUTS\n'+json.dumps(design,indent=2)+'\n\nMETHOD\n1.Freeze Stage03 combined thermal hardware, cap and mission.\n2.Reproduce P30 baseline.\n3.Compare P300 only.\n4.Test Ki0.1,0.5,2 with Kp300; back-calculation tracking60s, same300W cap.\n5.Select tested Ki2 on heater-on tracking/headroom criteria, then check air−10K and30s sensor lag.\n6.Check capacity100W diagnostic; controller cannot supply unavailable heat.\n7.Audit whole-system energy, native controller equations, periodicity and solver refinement.\n\nWHY ENERGY INCREASES\nThe baseline used less heat while running below its target. Removing that temperature deficit requires more heat. Motor-heater energy, all-heater energy and DC demand are distinct quantities; heater energy is already included in DC demand.\n\nRESULTS\n'+json.dumps(S,indent=2)+'\n\nREFINEMENT\n'+json.dumps(R,indent=2)+'\n\nBOUNDARIES\nContinuous ideal averaged heating; no hardware PWM, actuator delay, sensor bias/noise/failure or cold-soaked startup. Prescribed environmental/loss inputs and24 lumped thermal nodes. No physical correlation, component qualification or actual manufacturer hardware is claimed. Initial conditional-integration development attempt had poor numerical behavior at cut-off; its source/log/partial output are retained on Intel outside accepted results. Accepted results use back-calculation.\n\nMETHOD REFERENCE\nhttps://doc.modelica.org/om/Modelica.Blocks.Continuous.LimPID.html\n')
(B/'README.txt').write_text('STAGE04 / MOTOR HEATER CONTROL\n\nRead inputs/controller-design.json and docs/Results-Walkthrough.txt first.\n\nNative tools used:OpenModelica1.27.1, Modelica4.1.0, Python3/NumPy/SciPy/Matplotlib on Intel. From verification/native:omc ../../source/compile.mos. From project root:python3 source/run_cases.py then python3 source/audit_and_export.py. The reproduction check expects the immutable sibling folder stage-03-night-control-spatial-r1, including its results/combined_native.csv; download Stage03 combined full-native archive and extract there if reproducing elsewhere. inspect.mos produces native graph data for render_and_archive.py, which makes figures and archives.\n\nOpen source/HAPSDiurnal.mo in OMEdit, then IntegratedMission; open only one stage version at a time because the package name is shared.\n\nAll final-day CSVs and website JSONs are included. Separate full-native archives provide the main comparison and selected refinement; other complete8day CSVs remain on Intel, with hashes and runtime settings in verification/run-manifest.json. No compiled runtime binaries are distributed.\n\nPortable viewer:python3 -m http.server8894 --bind127.0.0.1, then open Review.html. The viewer inspects saved data and does not solve in-browser.\n')
local=body.replace('data-base="'+A+'"','data-base="."').replace(A+'/','');local=local.replace('href="#night-control"','href="https://khanisolutions.com/AISolutions/sceye-haps-thermal.html#night-control"').replace('href="#night-inputs"','href="https://khanisolutions.com/AISolutions/sceye-haps-thermal.html#night-inputs"').replace('href="#night-downloads"','href="https://khanisolutions.com/AISolutions/sceye-haps-thermal.html#night-downloads"')
(B/'Review.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Motor heater PI control / Stage04</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="review.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="source/motor.css"><body>'+local+'<script type="module" src="source/motor.mjs"></script></body></html>')
(B/'review.css').write_text('body{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:20px;font:17px/1.7 system-ui;color:#17394d;background:#f5f9fb}h2{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.2}section{margin:50px 0}.haps-box{padding:20px;background:white;border:1px solid #c5d8e1;border-radius:12px}.haps-jump{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap}a{color:#14627b}.eyebrow{font-size:.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}.haps-small{font-size:.86rem}button,select{font:inherit;color:#17394d;padding:10px;border:1px solid #9bb1bf;background:white;border-radius:8px}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#17677c;color:white}label{display:grid;gap:5px}select{max-width:100%}')
print('Built Stage04 report and page',m['minimum_housing_C'],m['peak_heater_W'],p['heater_energy_Wh']/1000)
